<%# Compound Interest result (spec issue #188, DESIGN.md §4). Composes BLEND components:
      • Hero-result — the future value (5px coral left rule, big tabular-nums), the answer.
      • Stat grid   — future value, total interest, principal (shared `.stat-grid`/`.stat-card`,
                      `--wide` track: future value runs to 7+ digits / cents on a big principal,
                      which would wrap at the default 9.5rem in the narrow result panel —
                      DESIGN.md §4 selection criteria for `--wide` money). Total interest is the
                      derived/positive figure → accent green (DESIGN.md §1).
      • Charts      — a Chart.js donut (principal vs. total interest, largest slice green,
                      hover tooltips) + a TradingView lightweight-charts area/line for the
                      year-by-year GROWTH curve (crosshair + per-point tooltip). Both keep an
                      always-rendered no-JS fallback (a text legend / an SVG curve) so the
                      breakdown never gates on JS and never relies on colour alone (DESIGN.md
                      §4 / §6); the Stimulus controller hides the fallback only once the live
                      chart has drawn.
    The backend owns every number (ARCHITECTURE.md §4); growth_series exists so the curve is
    drawn WITHOUT doing math. This only renders the envelope. `calc:` is a valid
    Calculators::CompoundInterest. %>
<% r = calc.result %>
<% future_value = r[:future_value] %>
<% total_interest = r[:total_interest] %>
<% principal = r[:principal] %>
<% series = r[:growth_series] %>
<% slices = compound_interest_donut(principal, total_interest) %>

<div class="space-y-6"
     data-controller="compound-interest"
     data-compound-interest-donut-value="<%= compound_interest_donut_data(slices).to_json %>"
     data-compound-interest-curve-value="<%= compound_interest_curve_data(series).to_json %>">
  <%# ── Hero: the future value ──────────────────────────────────────────────── %>
  <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)]">
    <div class="flex gap-5 p-7">
      <span class="w-[5px] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent">Future value</p>
        <p class="mt-2 flex items-baseline gap-1.5">
          <span class="text-sm font-bold text-faint">$</span>
          <span class="text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.04em] tabular-nums text-ink"><%= money_display(future_value) %></span>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          <span class="font-semibold text-accent">$<%= money_display(total_interest) %></span>
          earned on a $<%= money_display(principal) %> principal at
          <%= decimal_display(calc.annual_rate) %>% over <%= decimal_display(calc.years) %>
          <%= pluralize(calc.years, "year").split.last %>, compounding
          <span class="font-semibold text-ink"><%= compounding_label(r[:compounding]).downcase %></span>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# ── Stat grid: future value / total interest / principal ──────────────────
      The shared responsive stat grid (DESIGN.md §4 "Stat grid", issue #143): `.stat-grid` /
      `.stat-card` size each card to a min width and let the grid flow (≈3-across when wide,
      collapsing as it narrows). `--wide` (13rem) because the future value is a high-magnitude
      money figure — on a large principal it runs to 7+ digits + cents ($1,648,721.27), which
      wraps mid-number on the default 9.5rem track in the narrow result panel (DESIGN.md §4
      `--wide` money criterion). The `.stat-card dd` never-clip net (overflow-wrap) is the
      wrapping floor below that. Total interest is the derived/positive figure → accent green
      (DESIGN.md §1); future value + principal read in ink. %>
  <dl class="stat-grid stat-grid--wide">
    <div class="stat-card">
      <dt class="text-xs font-bold text-label">Future value</dt>
      <dd class="mt-1.5 text-xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.02em] tabular-nums text-ink break-words">$<%= money_display(future_value) %></dd>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-card">
      <dt class="text-xs font-bold text-label">Total interest</dt>
      <dd class="mt-1.5 text-xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.02em] tabular-nums text-accent break-words">+&nbsp;$<%= money_display(total_interest) %></dd>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-card">
      <dt class="text-xs font-bold text-label">Principal</dt>
      <dd class="mt-1.5 text-xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.02em] tabular-nums text-ink break-words">$<%= money_display(principal) %></dd>
    </div>
  </dl>

  <%# ── Charts: donut + growth curve (DESIGN.md §4 "Charts") ───────────────────
      Each chart is a [JS canvas (hidden until drawn)] + [static no-JS fallback (shown)].
      The Stimulus controller draws the live, hover-capable chart and only then hides the
      fallback. With no JS the fallback stays — the breakdown is reachable without JS and
      never colour-alone (DESIGN.md §4 / §6). %>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <%# Donut — principal vs. total interest. Chart.js draws the hover-tooltip doughnut;
        the figures repeat as a text legend below (always shown) so the breakdown reads
        without colour and without JS. %>
    <div class="rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface p-6 shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)]">
      <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-faint">Principal vs. interest</p>
      <div class="mt-4 flex items-center gap-5">
        <%# Live Chart.js donut canvas — hidden until the controller draws it. Explicit pixel
            dimensions (112×112 = the size-28 box) so Chart.js (responsive:false) sizes from
            the element, not a parent measured before layout reflows. %>
        <div class="relative size-28 shrink-0" data-compound-interest-target="donutCanvas" hidden>
          <canvas width="112" height="112" class="size-28"></canvas>
        </div>

        <%# No-JS fallback donut — a CSS conic-gradient from the two token colours (no inline
            hex; DESIGN.md §5 guardrail), largest slice green (DESIGN.md §1). %>
        <div class="relative size-28 shrink-0 rounded-full" role="img"
             data-compound-interest-target="donutFallback"
             aria-label="Principal $<%= money_display(principal) %>, total interest $<%= money_display(total_interest) %>"
             style="background: <%= compound_interest_donut_gradient(slices) %>;">
          <span class="absolute inset-[22%] rounded-full bg-surface" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </div>

        <%# Text legend (always shown) — the breakdown without colour (DESIGN.md §6). %>
        <dl class="min-w-0 flex-1 space-y-3">
          <% slices.each do |slice| %>
            <div>
              <dt class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-bold text-label">
                <span class="inline-block size-2.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-<%= slice[:color] %>" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <%= slice[:label] %>
              </dt>
              <dd class="mt-0.5 pl-4.5 text-lg font-extrabold tabular-nums text-ink">$<%= money_display(slice[:amount]) %></dd>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# Growth over time — lightweight-charts draws the crosshair+tooltip area/line into the
        canvas; the no-JS fallback is an SVG area+line from the same backend samples, with the
        endpoints labelled so the trend reads without colour or JS. %>
    <div class="rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface p-6 shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)]">
      <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-faint">Growth over time</p>

      <%# Live lightweight-charts canvas — hidden until the controller draws it. %>
      <div class="mt-4 h-32 w-full" data-compound-interest-target="curveCanvas" hidden></div>

      <%# No-JS fallback — the SVG curve + endpoint labels (DESIGN.md §6: not colour-alone).
          The balance rises, so the area is anchored to the bottom and the line climbs. %>
      <div data-compound-interest-target="curveFallback">
        <% points = compound_interest_curve_points(series) %>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" preserveAspectRatio="none" class="mt-4 h-28 w-full" role="img"
             aria-label="Balance growing from $<%= money_display(series.first[:balance]) %> to $<%= money_display(series.last[:balance]) %> over the term">
          <polygon points="0,100 <%= points %> 100,100" fill="var(--color-accent)" fill-opacity="0.12" />
          <polyline points="<%= points %>" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-accent)" stroke-width="2"
                    vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
        </svg>
        <div class="mt-3 flex items-baseline justify-between text-xs font-semibold text-faint">
          <span class="tabular-nums">$<%= money_display(series.first[:balance]) %></span>
          <span class="tabular-nums">$<%= money_display(series.last[:balance]) %></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# ── Growth schedule (DESIGN.md §4 "Data table") ─────────────────────────────
      The year-by-year balance — the no-JS-reachable data behind the curve (DESIGN.md §4:
      the chart enhances the numbers, never gates access to them). Thin rule borders,
      right-aligned tabular-nums, a hard ink total row. One row per year (short), so no
      pagination. Every figure is the backend's (the growth_series balances) — the FE does
      no math (ARCHITECTURE.md §4). %>
  <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)]">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-2 px-6 pt-6">
      <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-faint">Year-by-year balance</p>
      <p class="text-xs text-muted tabular-nums"><%= pluralize(series.length, "point") %></p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 max-h-[28rem] overflow-y-auto">
      <table class="w-full text-sm">
        <thead class="sticky top-0 z-10 bg-surface">
          <tr class="border-b border-rule text-left text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-faint">
            <th scope="col" class="px-6 py-2.5 font-bold">Year</th>
            <th scope="col" class="px-6 py-2.5 text-right font-bold">Balance</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <% series.each do |point| %>
            <tr class="border-b border-rule/70 text-ink last:border-0">
              <td class="px-6 py-2.5 tabular-nums text-muted"><%= point[:year] %></td>
              <td class="px-6 py-2.5 text-right tabular-nums">$<%= money_display(point[:balance]) %></td>
            </tr>
          <% end %>
        </tbody>
        <tfoot>
          <%# Hard total row — top border in ink (DESIGN.md §4 "Data table"). The future
              value (final balance) + the total interest earned over the whole term. %>
          <tr class="border-t-2 border-ink bg-bg/40 font-bold text-ink">
            <td class="px-6 py-3">Final balance</td>
            <td class="px-6 py-3 text-right tabular-nums">$<%= money_display(future_value) %></td>
          </tr>
        </tfoot>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
